{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:42821620 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:42821620 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"42821620","source":"MED","pmid":"42821620","pmcid":"PMC13652322","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13652322"]},"doi":"10.1371/journal.pntd.0014104","title":"Microfilaremic loiasis is associated with T cell hyporesponsiveness against SARS-CoV-2.","authorString":"Augé Stock M, Okwu DG, More A, Doralt A, Bikangui R, Boussoukou IPM, Eberhardt KA, Sandkuhl M, Zoleko Manego R, Mombo-Ngoma G, McCall M, Breloer M, Esen M, Addo M, Lell B, Veletzky L, Adamou R, Mackroth MS.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Augé Stock M","lastName":"Augé Stock","firstName":"Maximilian","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."},{"affiliation":"Department of Medicine I, Division of Infectious Diseases and Tropical Medicine, Medical University of Vienna, Vienna, Austria."},{"affiliation":"I, Department of Medicine, Division of Infectious Diseases, University Medical Centre Hamburg-Eppendorf, Hamburg, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Okwu DG","lastName":"Okwu","firstName":"Dearie Glory","initials":"DG","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."}]}},{"fullName":"More A","lastName":"More","firstName":"Ayong","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."}]}},{"fullName":"Doralt A","lastName":"Doralt","firstName":"Anna","initials":"A","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."}]}},{"fullName":"Bikangui R","lastName":"Bikangui","firstName":"Rodrigue","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."}]}},{"fullName":"Boussoukou IPM","lastName":"Boussoukou","firstName":"Ismaël Pierrick Mikelet","initials":"IPM","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."}]}},{"fullName":"Eberhardt KA","lastName":"Eberhardt","firstName":"Kirsten Alexandra","initials":"KA","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Gastroenterology, Hepatology and Infectious Diseases, Medical Faculty and University Hospital Düsseldorf, Heinrich Heine University Düsseldorf, Düsseldorf, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Sandkuhl M","lastName":"Sandkuhl","firstName":"Maren","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"I, Department of Medicine, Division of Infectious Diseases, University Medical Centre Hamburg-Eppendorf, Hamburg, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Protozoa Immunology Group, Bernhard Nocht Institute for Tropical Medicine, Hamburg, Germany."},{"affiliation":"German Centre for Infection Research, Partner Sites Hamburg-Lübeck, Borstel-Riems, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Zoleko Manego R","lastName":"Zoleko Manego","firstName":"Rella","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."},{"affiliation":"German Centre for Infection Research, Partner Sites Hamburg-Lübeck, Borstel-Riems, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Drug Implementation Research Group, Bernhard Nocht Institute for Tropical Medicine, and I, Department of Medicine, University Medical Centre Hamburg-Eppendorf, Hamburg, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Mombo-Ngoma G","lastName":"Mombo-Ngoma","firstName":"Ghyslain","initials":"G","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."},{"affiliation":"German Centre for Infection Research, Partner Sites Hamburg-Lübeck, Borstel-Riems, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Drug Implementation Research Group, Bernhard Nocht Institute for Tropical Medicine, and I, Department of Medicine, University Medical Centre Hamburg-Eppendorf, Hamburg, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"McCall M","lastName":"McCall","firstName":"Matthew","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."},{"affiliation":"Radboud University Medical Center, Department of Medical Microbiology, Nijmegen, The Netherlands."}]}},{"fullName":"Breloer M","lastName":"Breloer","firstName":"Minka","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Section Interface, Helminth Immunology Group, Bernhard Nocht Institute for Tropical Medicine, Hamburg, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Department of Biology, University Hamburg, Hamburg, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Esen M","lastName":"Esen","firstName":"Meral","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."},{"affiliation":"Institute of Tropical Medicine, University of Tübingen, Tübingen, Germany."},{"affiliation":"German Center for Infection and Research (DZIF), Partner site Tübingen, Tübingen, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Addo M","lastName":"Addo","firstName":"Marylyn","initials":"M","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"I, Department of Medicine, Division of Infectious Diseases, University Medical Centre Hamburg-Eppendorf, Hamburg, Germany."},{"affiliation":"German Centre for Infection Research, Partner Sites Hamburg-Lübeck, Borstel-Riems, Germany."}]}},{"fullName":"Lell B","lastName":"Lell","firstName":"Bertrand","initials":"B","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."},{"affiliation":"Department of Medicine I, Division of Infectious Diseases and Tropical Medicine, Medical University of Vienna, Vienna, Austria."}]}},{"fullName":"Veletzky L","lastName":"Veletzky","firstName":"Luzia","initials":"L","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."},{"affiliation":"Department of Medicine I, Division of Infectious Diseases and Tropical Medicine, Medical University of Vienna, Vienna, Austria."}]}},{"fullName":"Adamou R","lastName":"Adamou","firstName":"Rafiou","initials":"R","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon."}]}},{"fullName":"Mackroth MS","lastName":"Mackroth","firstName":"Maria Sophia","initials":"MS","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5178-8297"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"I, Department of Medicine, Division of Infectious Diseases, University Medical Centre Hamburg-Eppendorf, Hamburg, Germany."},{"affiliation":"Protozoa Immunology Group, Bernhard Nocht Institute for Tropical Medicine, Hamburg, Germany."},{"affiliation":"German Centre for Infection Research, Partner Sites Hamburg-Lübeck, Borstel-Riems, Germany."},{"affiliation":"MSH Medical School Hamburg, Institute for Translational Medicine, Hamburg, Germany."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0000-0001-5178-8297"}]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"10","volume":"20","journalIssueId":4275853,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"PLoS Negl Trop Dis","title":"PLoS neglected tropical diseases","essn":"1935-2735","issn":"1935-2727","isoabbreviation":"PLoS Negl Trop Dis","nlmid":"101291488"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-10-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e0014104","abstractText":"<h4>Background</h4>Loiasis is a chronic filarial infection endemic to Central and West Africa. Although long considered benign, increasing evidence links loiasis to substantial morbidity and mortality. The infection is associated with immune modulation, including Th2-skewed responses and elevated regulatory cytokines. Clinically, loiasis is classified as microfilaremic (presence of circulating microfilariae) or amicrofilaremic (\"occult\") disease, the latter defined by a history of eyeworm migration without detectable microfilaremia. This study investigated how chronic L. loa infection influences antibody and T cell responses to SARS-CoV-2 following natural infection.<h4>Methods</h4>Between 2022 and 2024, this cross-sectional study was done in rural and periurban villages of the Ngounié and Moyen-Ogooué provinces of Gabon. Study procedures included diagnostics for loiasis and immunological assays. Microfilaremia was confirmed by stained blood smear microscopy, and occult disease was identified using the Rapid Assessment Procedure for Loiasis. SARS-CoV-2-specific IgG responses to spike and nucleocapsid proteins were measured by ELISA, and IFN-γ responses to spike antigen were assessed using an interferon-gamma release assay.<h4>Results</h4>Overall, 192 participants were categorized as microfilaremic (n = 43), occult loiasis (n = 59), or without evidence of active loiasis (n = 90). IFN-γ responses were reduced in microfilaremic individuals compared with other participants (p = 0.031), whereas IgG responses did not differ. Subsequent analysis across the three groups confirmed that IFN-γ responses were lower in microfilaremic compared with occult participants (p = 0.012).<h4>Conclusion</h4>These findings suggest that microfilaremic loiasis may impair proinflammatory T cell responses to viral antigens, highlighting the need for further research into the broader immunological effects of Loa loa infection in endemic populations.","affiliation":"Centre de Recherches Médicales de Lambaréné, Lambaréné, Gabon.","publicationStatus":"aheadofprint","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print-Electronic","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pntd.0014104"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13652322"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13652322?pdf=render"}]},"commentCorrectionList":{"commentCorrection":[{"source":"PPR","id":"PPR1221430","type":"Preprint in","note":"Link created based on a title-first author match","orderIn":10002}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"N","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"Y","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"N","dateOfCreation":"2026-10-01","dateOfRevision":"2026-10-01","electronicPublicationDate":"2026-10-01","firstPublicationDate":"2026-10-01","firstIndexDate":"2026-10-02","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-10-10","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}